:PNLGRP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME=PRGJRNRCV.Purge Journal Recievers
:P.This command is used to purge old joural receivers before a specified
number of days. It allows for selection of receiver by name and library
and it includes optons for wildcards and excluding libraries.
:P.It prints a report of what was purged and has the option to include
receiver not being purged. It can also be run without doing the purge
to preview what is going to happen when the purge option is run.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='PRGJRNRCV/JRNRCV'.Journal Receiver
:XH3.JRNRCV - Journal Receiver
:P.Specifies the name and library of the journal receiver or receivers
being deleted.
:p.This is a required parameter.

:H3.Qualifier 1: Journal receiver
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.journal-receiver-name:EPK.
:PD.Specify the name and library of the journal receiver
being deleted.  If *LIBL or *USRLIBL is specified for
the library name, only the first journal receiver
found to have this name is deleted.  If *ALLUSR or
*ALL is specified for the library name, journal
receiver objects by the name specified can be deleted
from multiple libraries.

:PT.:PK.generic*-journal-receiver-name:EPK.
:PD.
Specify the generic name of the journal receiver being deleted.  A
generic name is a character string that contains one or more
characters followed by an asterisk (*); for example, ABC*.  The
asterisk substitutes for any valid characters.  A generic name
specifies all objects with names that begin with the generic prefix
for which the user has authority.  If an asterisk is not included
with the generic (prefix) name, the system assumes it to be the
complete object name.
:EPARML.

:H3.Qualifier 2: Library

:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.All libraries in the library list for the current thread are
searched until the first match is found.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library for the thread is searched.  If no library is
specified as the current library for the thread, the QGPL library is
searched.
:PT.:PK.*USRLIBL:EPK.
:PD.If a current library entry exists in the library list for the
current thread, the current library and the libraries in the user
portion of the library list are searched.  If there is no current
library entry, only the libraries in the user portion of the library
list are searched.
:PT.:PK.*ALLUSR:EPK.
:PD.All user libraries are searched.  All libraries with names that do
not begin with the letter Q are searched except for the following:
:XMP.
#CGULIB     #DSULIB     #SEULIB
#COBLIB     #RPGLIB
#DFULIB     #SDALIB
:EXMP.
:P.Although the following Qxxx libraries are provided by IBM, they
typically contain user data that changes frequently.  Therefore,
these libraries are considered user libraries and are also searched:

:XMP.
QDSNX       QRCLxxxxx   QUSRDIRDB   QUSRVI
QGPL        QSRVAGT     QUSRIJS     QUSRVxRxMx
QGPL38      QSYS2       QUSRINFSKR  QWQCENT
QMGTC       QSYS2xxxxx  QUSRNOTES   QWQREPOS
QMGTC2      QS36F       QUSROND
QMPGDATA    QUSER38     QUSRPOSGS
QMQMDATA    QUSRADSM    QUSRPOSSA
QMQMPROC    QUSRBRM     QUSRPYMSVR
QPFRDATA    QUSRDIRCF   QUSRRDARS
QRCL        QUSRDIRCL   QUSRSYS
:EXMP.

:ol.:li.'xxxxx' is the number of a primary auxiliary storage pool (ASP).
    :li.A different library name, in the format QUSRVxRxMx, can be
created by the user for each previous release supported by IBM
to contain any user commands to be compiled in a CL program
for the previous release.  For the QUSRVxRxMx user library,
VxRxMx is the version, release, and modification level of a
previous release that IBM continues to support.
:EOL.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All libraries in the system, including QSYS, are searched.

:PT.:PK. name:EPK.
:PD.Specify the name of the library to be searched.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='PRGJRNRCV/PRGDAYS'.Days Old to Purge
:XH3.PRGDAYS - Days Old to Purge
:P.Enter the number of days old to purge. For exmaple, 30 will purge
entries that have been detached for over 30 days before today and are saved.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='PRGJRNRCV/PURGE'.Purge Receivers
:XH3.PURGE - Purge Receivers
:P.This option allows the purge program to not purge. This allows the user
to view the purge report before actually purgin the entries.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK def.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Purges selected entries.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.Prints the purge list, but does not purge any receivers.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='PRGJRNRCV/PRGUNSAVED'.Purge Un-Saved Journals
:XH3.PRGUNSAVED - Purge Un-Saved Journals
:P.This option allows puring of entries that have not been saved.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK def.*NO:EPK.
:PD.Unsaved entries are not purged.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Unsaved entries are purged.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='PRGJRNRCV/EXCLIB'.Exclude Libraries
:XH3.EXCLIB - Exclude Libraries
:P.This allows a list of libraries to excluded from the search.
:p.This can be used have seperate purging logic for specific libraries
then the whole system.
:p.For exmaple, you may want to purge all saved jounals after 60 days
for most libraries, but keep journals for your primary data library for 120
days. Assuming your primary data library is MYDATAJRN you could use this
command twice. One including all libraries except MYDATAJRN and once just using
MYDATA.
:p.The following examples show how this would be done.
:XMP.

/* Purge all recievers except data library, older than 60 days */
   PRGJRNRCV JRNRCV(*ALL/*ALL) PRGDAYS(60) EXCLIB(MYDATAJRN)

/* Purge the data library receivers older than 120 days */
   PRGJRNRCV JRNRCV(MYDATAJRN/*ALL) PRGDAYS(120)

:EXMP.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='PRGJRNRCV/PRTOPT'.Print Option
:XH3.PRTOPT - Print Option
:P.This option determines what is included on the report.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK def.*PURGED:EPK.
:PD.This option only prints journal receivers that are purged.
:PT.:PK.*SAVED:EPK.
:PD.This option will print all journals that have been saved and are
no longer active. It will still only purge entries before the entered
number of days. The detached saved entries after the purge date will
be marked as not purged on the report.
:PT.:Pk.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.The *ALL option print all journal receivers within the selection
criteria. It will still only purge entries before the entered
number of days that have been detached and saved. Each entry that
is not purged will show so in the message column.
:PT.:Pk.*NOLIST:EPK.
:PD.This option will run the purge but no listing will
be produced.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:EPNLGRP.
